<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Mean of ungrouped data using an assumed mean</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The masses, in kg, of \(8\) sacks of maize at a cereals depot in Eldoret are</p><p style="text-align:center;">\({@xs[1]@},\ {@xs[2]@},\ {@xs[3]@},\ {@xs[4]@},\ {@xs[5]@},\ {@xs[6]@},\ {@xs[7]@},\ {@xs[8]@}\)</p><p>Use the assumed mean \(A = {@A@}\) kg.</p><p>(a) Find \(\Sigma d\), where \(d = x - A\).</p><div>\(\Sigma d =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the mean mass, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><div>Mean \(=\) [[input:ans2]] kg [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>With an assumed mean, subtract the same number \(A\) from every value to get the deviations \(d = x - A\), keeping their signs. Subtracting the same number \(A\) from every value moves the mean down by \(A\) and leaves the spread unchanged, so the mean of the deviations, \(\Sigma d \div n\), is how far the true mean lies above (or below) \(A\).</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Mass \(x\) (kg)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xs[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xs[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xs[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xs[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xs[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xs[6]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xs[7]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@xs[8]@}</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(d = x - {@A@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@d[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@d[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@d[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@d[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@d[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@d[6]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@d[7]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@d[8]@}</td></tr></table><p>(a) Adding the deviations, \(\Sigma d = {@Sd@}\).</p><p>(b) \[\bar{x} = A + \frac{\Sigma d}{n} = {@A@} [[if test="is(Sd>=0)"]]+[[else]]-[[/if]] \frac{ {@aSd@} }{8} = {@exd(mn)@}\]The mean mass is about \({@mnd@}\) kg.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* exd: shortest exact decimal display of a terminating value (up to 3 d.p.) */
exd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else dispdp(float(v),3);
/* Design: code, find the mean, decode; subtraction only. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Statistics 1, chapter 2, section A, A6. */
dlist: [[-3,3,-5,2,6,4,4,0],[4,3,-2,-2,-5,1,-2,-4],[4,2,0,4,-1,6,4,-4],[-5,2,3,0,1,-4,-5,-5],[-4,-3,4,-6,-6,-3,7,0],[-7,-6,-5,4,5,-1,3,-4],[-1,-6,2,5,-5,5,-7,-6],[-3,-5,-6,-4,-7,2,7,-3],[-4,5,-4,5,3,0,-1,6],[-5,5,4,0,-4,0,-7,4]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
d: dlist[ix];
A: rand([86,88,90,92,94]);
xs: makelist(A+d[k],k,1,8);
Sd: apply("+",d);
mn: A+Sd/8;
mnd: dispdp(float(floor(10^1*(mn)+1/2)/10^1),1);
/* diagnostics */
negSd: -Sd;
absSd: apply("+",map(abs,d));
dbar: Sd/8;
mnsign: A-Sd/8;
mnnodiv: A+Sd;
/* test values */
mn1: float(floor(10^1*(mn)+1/2)/10^1);
mnsign1: float(floor(10^1*(mnsign)+1/2)/10^1);
dbar1: float(floor(10^1*(dbar)+1/2)/10^1);
ft1: float(floor(10^1*(A+(Sd+8)/8)+1/2)/10^1);
aSd: abs(Sd);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
