  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Statistics II: mean using an assumed mean</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 3.1: Find the sum of the deviations from a given assumed mean, and the mean of ungrouped data.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question A6 in Section A of Chapter 2 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P. and Shilton, S., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Statistics 1 for Edexcel, Cambridge University Press, 2004: the coding is reduced to subtracting an assumed mean, with a new Kenyan context and new data.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
